{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/990878-using-practice-as-instrument","id":990878,"title":"Using Practice...as Instrument?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-21T03:28:21-07:00","id":990878,"title":"Using Practice...as Instrument?","content":"This is a point that's been bugging me lately, so I started rereading the passage in M20 about Violence as Focus. Then, I read this line on p. 415:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>M20</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">...John Courage puts his Black Suit training to good use. [John Courage's Player] declares that he\u2019s <b><i>using the martial arts practice as a focus</i></b>, rolls his Enlightenment Trait, and scores four successes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Now this seems like a &quot;no duh&quot; moment, since Martial Arts is a Practice that can be a part of one's Focus. But keep in mind, nowhere in M20's list of Instruments is listed &quot;hand to hand combat&quot; or &quot;Martial Arts&quot;. Weapons are listed, but the description left no indication that this included unarmed maneuvers.<br /> <br /> So this seems to imply that, in absence of any specific Instrument listed, one can use their general <i>Practice</i> as an Instrument. I may be wrong on this point, but it's perplexing. That's not how Focus works otherwise in M20 - the way the word used to be used is now called Instrument, obviously.<br /> <br /> And if using Practice as Instrument were true - and it seems to be from context - is this limited to the Martial Arts Practice? Or are their cases where other Practices could stand in for Instruments? And how would that even work?<br /> <br /> What do you people think?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T03:41:37-07:00","id":990885,"title":"","content":"Instruments listed (pg 566) include meditation, ordeals and exertions, prayers and invocations, sex and sensuality, social domination, voice and vocalizations, bodywork, dances and movement, and eye contact. Given those as examples, martial arts should be usable as an instrument as well as a practice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T03:48:35-07:00","id":990887,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/990878-using-practice-as-instrument?p=990885#post990885\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Instruments listed (pg 566) include meditation, ordeals and exertions, prayers and invocations, sex and sensuality, social domination, voice and vocalizations, bodywork, dances and movement, and eye contact. Given those as examples, martial arts should be usable as an instrument as well as a practice.</div> </div> </div> </div>But is &quot;Punch&quot; on that list? Some would argue yes (dance and movement). I would argue no.<br /> <br /> Not that I suppose it matters. Even if we accept the Martial Arts Practice as, in and of itself, a viable Instrument in everything but name, it's not like it's unbalancing. While there's a minimum of Instruments a character must take, there's no upper limit mandated. There could have been a Martial Arts entry on the Instrument list for all the difference it made.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T03:52:04-07:00","id":990888,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/990878-using-practice-as-instrument?p=990887#post990887\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But is &quot;Punch&quot; on that list? Some would argue yes (dance and movement). I would argue no.<br /> <br /> Not that I suppose it matters. Even if we accept the Martial Arts Practice as, in and of itself, a viable Instrument in everything but name, it's not like it's unbalancing. While there's a minimum of Instruments a character must take, there's no upper limit mandated. There could have been a Martial Arts entry on the Instrument list for all the difference it made.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I would argue in return that the list is descriptive, not prescriptive. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T11:02:13-07:00","id":991037,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/990878-using-practice-as-instrument?p=990888#post990888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, I would argue in return that the list is descriptive, not prescriptive. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>This, people already complain about the word count of M20 and listing every possible permutation of practices and instruments is madness. Additionally under the ordeals and exertions section of the instruments it lists some while following the list with an ellipses meaning that those are not the only options (and one of the options they do list is cage-fighing putting more credence to combat as an instrument). Martial Arts is a practice and the use of punches, kicks, blocks, kata... are its instruments the same way that Faith is a practice and Prayer and Invocations are examples of its instruments.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2008-cynic01","name":"Cynic01","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"437"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T11:04:29-07:00","id":991038,"title":"","content":"Practice is essentially the same as Preparation.<br /> A Black Suit has procedures he can use simply because of special training (=practice/=preparation)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T12:45:52-07:00","id":991070,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nonsense</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/990878-using-practice-as-instrument?p=991038#post991038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Practice is essentially the same as Preparation.<br /> A Black Suit has procedures he can use simply because of special training (=practice/=preparation)</div> </div> </div> </div>Going to build off this and the idea of Martial Arts to be used as a Focus. Martial Arts is more than just a way to punch somebody in the face, it's also mental &quot;preparation and with the NWO good at mind it fits. Now if John Courage wants to get in a street brawl this wouldn't fit but if he want's to clear his mind for some reason then yes it would.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9486-jbrocky","name":"JBRocky","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9486_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T23:09:25-07:00","id":991297,"title":"","content":"The NWO is actually the Convention that is the most inclined to regularly get into martial arts training, as per RAW.<br /> Heck, M20 explains how things like meditation and yoga are no stranger to them, and they have written rotes for making use of some quite impressive hand-to-hand things along those lines.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 10-22-2016, 02:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}